.TH TIMERC 1 "2026" "timerc 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timerc, timerc-bg \- native X11 countdown timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timerc
[\fItime\fR] [\fItask\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B timerc-bg
[\fItime\fR] [\fItask\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B timerc
.RB { config | insights | about }
[\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B timerc test
.RB { alarm | preparing | sleeping | waking | all }
.br
.B timerc /testsleep
.I time
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timerc
is a small countdown timer written in C for X11.
The graphical window does exactly three things: it takes your input, shows the
running timer, and rings the alarm. Everything else (settings, statistics,
help, audio tests) is in the terminal; see
.BR timerc-config (1),
.BR timerc-insights (1)
and
.B TERMINAL UIS
below.
.PP
.B timerc
runs in the foreground and blocks until the timer ends, so it is usable in
scripts:
.B timerc 5m && notify-send done
.PP
.B timerc-bg
is the same program (it is selected by the name it is run under) detached from
the terminal like a daemon; see
.BR timerc-bg (1).
.PP
With no time argument the setup window opens.
.SH TIME FORMATS
.TP
.B 25m, 1h30m, 90s, 500ms
Durations. A bare number is minutes.
.TP
.B 30:00, 1:30:00
Clock-style durations (mm:ss, h:mm:ss).
.TP
.B u15:30
Until the clock reads 15:30 (today, or tomorrow if already past).
.TP
.B u:30
Until minute 30 of this (or the next) hour.
.PP
Anything after the time is the task name shown on the timer and in statistics.
.SH SWITCHES
Single letters written before the time, with or without a space, and combinable
(\fBfp25m\fR):
.TP
.B d
Shut the machine down when the timer ends.
.TP
.B a
Fullscreen alert when the timer ends (the default mode).
.TP
.B f, r
Start fullscreen.
.TP
.B p
Pausable: Space or left click pauses and resumes.
.TP
.B l
Lock keyboard and mouse until the timer ends (needs \fBtimerc-lock-helper\fR).
.TP
.B /
Sleep mode: ambient audio that fades in, sustains, then wakes you gently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " alert|shutdown"
Mode when the timer ends.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pausable
Allow pause/resume.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lock
Disconnect USB keyboard/mouse (needs timerc-lock-helper).
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Select a theme by name.
.TP
.B \-\-gl
Use the OpenGL renderer when built with it.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH WINDOW CONTROLS
.TP
.B Setup window
Enter starts, Tab (or Ctrl+T) rolls a new theme, Ctrl+A moves the cursor to the
end, Esc quits.
.TP
.B Running timer
Space or left click: pause/resume (with \fBp\fR). Right click: toggle mini and
fullscreen. Middle click: stop. Drag the mini window to move it, drag its
corner to resize.
.TP
.B Alert
Esc or any click dismisses it.
.SH TERMINAL UIS
.TP
.B timerc config
Interactive settings and audio tests; also scriptable. See
.BR timerc-config (1).
.TP
.B timerc insights
Session statistics and event log. See
.BR timerc-insights (1).
.TP
.B timerc about
Syntax, keys and credits (plain text when not on a terminal).
.TP
.BI "timerc test " "alarm|preparing|sleeping|waking|all"
Plays the procedurally generated audio at the configured volume (30 s per phase).
.TP
.BI "timerc /testsleep " time
Prints the sleep-mode phase plan for that duration without playing anything.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY, XAUTHORITY
X server to use. When \fBDISPLAY\fR is unset (for example over SSH),
.B timerc
looks for a running graphical session of the same user and adopts its values.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in the terminal UIs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/timerc/config.conf
Settings, one \fBkey = value\fR per line (edit with \fBtimerc config\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.config/timerc/data.db
SQLite database of sessions and events.
.TP
.I ~/.config/timerc/timer.log
Log file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (the timer ran to its end or was dismissed), non-zero on invalid
arguments or when the X display cannot be opened.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
timerc 25m write report
timerc-bg u16:30 meeting
timerc pf45m deep work
timerc /8h
timerc config set alarm_volume_max_percent 60
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timerc-bg (1),
.BR timerc-config (1),
.BR timerc-insights (1)
.PP
https://github.com/mkalmousli/timerc
